==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Tampon with applicator.jpg|thumb|A tampon with an applicator]]

===Etymology===
{{etydate|1848}} Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|tampon}}, from {{der|en|frm|tampion}}, a nasalised variant of {{m|frm|tapon}}, a diminutive or augmented form of {{der|en|fro|tape|t=plug, bung, tap}}, from {{der|en|frk|*tappo|t=stopper, plug}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*tappô|t=plug, tap}}. Cognate with {{cog|goh|zapfo||stopper}}, {{cog|ang|tæppa||stopper}}. More at {{l|en|tap}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|[ˈtʰæmpɒn]|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tampon.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|[ˈtʰæmpɑn]|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|æmpɑn|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[plug]] of [[cotton]] or other [[absorbent]] material [[inserted]] into a [[body cavity]] or wound to [[absorb]] fluid, especially one inserted in the [[vagina]] during [[menstruation]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1988|author=w:Tsitsi Dangarembga|title=w:Nervous Conditions|publisher=Faber & Faber Limited (2021)|page=145|passage=I examined a '''tampon''', from the outside only without removing the wrapper because I did not want to waste one, and considered aloud the consequences of pushing the offensively shaped object into my vagina.}}
# A double-headed [[drumstick]] primarily for the [[bass drum]].
# An [[ink]]ing [[pad]] used in [[lithographic]] [[printing]].

